    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "But who told ninja that foo.o depends on foo.h? The compiler, via a depfile.",
      "narration": "The rule has the compiler write a depfile. With deps equals gcc, ninja parses it and stores the header list in its binary deps log.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Discovered deps",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 8,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "rule cc\n  command = clang -MD -MF $out.d ...\n  depfile = $out.d\n  deps = gcc",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 18,
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "hl",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "c",
          "at": 4500,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Headers are recorded in .ninja_deps, not re-parsed from makefiles",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 46,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 14,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 6000,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": ".ninja_log stores a hash of each command, so changed flags also trigger a rebuild.",
      "narration": "The ninja log stores a hash of each command line per output. Change a compiler flag and the hash differs, so the edge rebuilds.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Dirty checks",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 8,
          "at": 0,
